Rehomed here (2026-08-06): deferred ".." path-semantics alternative
---------------------------------------------------------------------
From cad-path-dotdot-resolution.issue (now CLOSED): clautolisp currently
does POSIX-UP for ".." on every platform and warns on any ".." outside
--lax (shipped 1.7.5). The probe matrix showed the native Windows CADs
(AutoCAD-Windows, BricsCAD-Windows) instead do syntactic-BACK, while
macOS BricsCAD and clautolisp everywhere do UP. A deferred alternative
was recorded but not scheduled: make clautolisp FOLLOW THE PLATFORM —
BACK on Windows, UP on Unix — so it matches whichever native CAD runs
beside it, at the cost of cross-OS clautolisp consistency. This is a
platform-dependent path-semantics choice on the same platform axis as the
"/..."-warns-on-autocad-windows case above, hence tracked here. Revisit if
the Windows divergence proves a problem in practice; not scheduled now.
